.TH "FLOX\-SEARCH" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-search \- search for packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general options>] search
     [\-\-json]
     [\-a]
     <search\-term>
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search for available packages.
.PP
A limited number of search results are reported by default for brevity.
The full result set can be returned via the \f[CR]\-a\f[R] flag.
.PP
Only the package name and description are shown by default.
Structured search results can be returned via the \f[CR]\-\-json\f[R]
flag.
More specific information for a single package is available via the
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-show(1)\f[B]\f[R] command.
.SS Package names
Packages are organized in a hierarchical structure such that certain
packages are found at the top level (e.g.\ \f[CR]ripgrep\f[R]), and
other packages are found under package sets
(e.g.\ \f[CR]python310Packages.pip\f[R]).
We call this location within the catalog the \(lqpkg\-path\(rq.
.PP
The pkg\-path is searched when you execute a \f[CR]flox search\f[R]
command.
The pkg\-path is what\(cqs shown by \f[CR]flox show\f[R].
Finally, the pkg\-path appears in your manifest after a
\f[CR]flox install\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B][install]\f[R]
ripgrep.pkg\-path = \(dqripgrep\(dq
pip.pkg\-path = \(dqpython310Packages.pip\(dq
.EE
.SS Fuzzy search
\f[CR]flox search\f[R] uses a fuzzy search mechanism that tries to match
either some portion of the pkg\-path or description.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Search Options
.TP
\f[CR]<search\-term>\f[R]
The package name to search for.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-json\f[R]
Display the search results in JSON format.
.TP
\f[CR]\-a\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-all\f[R]
Display all search results (default: at most 10).
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
